analysis of data points collected over time to understand patterns and future behaviour.

structure:
- trend [ long term movement in data ]
- seasonality [ patterns repeating at regular intervals ]
- cyclic behaviour [ long term oscillations ]
- randomness [ unpredictable fluctuations ]

types:
- univariate [ only 1 variable changes overtime ]
- multivariate [ multiple variables evolve together ]

stationarity: constant mean, variance and autocorrelation structure
non stationary data: trends, changing variances, structural breaks

autocorrelation: measures how current values relate to past values

forecasting steps:
- collect data
- visualize data
- check stationarity
- tranform data if needed
- choose model
- train model
- test accuracy
- forecast future values
